    docs(node): layer 30 has no bus worker and layer 90 writes the manifest, not a digest
    
    specs/NODE.md's layer table named two capabilities as shipped behaviour that no shipped layer
    establishes: layer 30 "a crier identity file (600) and a pull worker", layer 90 "one round trip
    whose digest is recomputed on the control host".
    
    scripts/project-node.sh:241-252 prints only crier_identity and crier_mode for layer 30 — no
    process, no socket, no worker query — and :288-316 prints only "[90] manifest" and writes
    $HOME/.node/node.json. grep -c digest scripts/project-node.sh prints 0.
    
    The cells now name what the ladder measures, and a paragraph under the table records the unshipped
    round trip (CF-004) and layer 30's file-existence weakness (CF-068) as not measured. Layer 40's
    cell was narrowed the same way in 6f75e28 (CF-032); layers 30 and 90 were left behind, so the spec
    contradicted docs/OPERATIONS.md sections 5-6 and AGENTS.md rule 1 had no owner for it.
    
    Evidence: docs/audits/code-factory-docs-2026-11-04.md — three layer-30 arms (identity absent, mode
    600, mode 644), the layer-90 check row, the grep output, SELFTEST: PASS and boardctl RESULT: OK at
    e657d98. Not measured by this change: whether any bus worker runs on a node, and the control-host
    digest round trip.
    
    Guard: this is a fresh clone with no pre-commit hook installed, so no hook ran at commit time; the
    Tier-1/Tier-2 battery runs through gitreins task complete (CF-079-DOC1) on this commit.
    
    Addresses CF-079.
